f("major", "50-act.json DM-ACT-REFER-GLU-01 (needs glucose_goal_unmet_on_oral); DM-ACT-RX-02/-03/-04 notWhen GLU18; 10-suspect.json DM-SUS-INCID-01",
  "A glucose of 18 or more after a negative ketone test reaches no referral unless one optional box is ticked. Evaluator (own3 P21): known type 2 on metformin, meter 25, urine ketones neg, goal field blank -> NOTHING fires; RX-04 is 'suppressed' by the notWhen 'WHO refers... the referral rule applies', but the referral rule did not fire. P22: new adult at a district site, meter 25, asymptomatic, ketones neg -> only DM-SUS-INCID-01 routine 'repeat on another day'.",
  "The pack's own REF-DM-ACU-KETONE-TEST-GLU quotes WHO PEN: 'Refer to hospital all patients with plasma glucose levels >= 18 mmol/l'; HEARTS-D Fig. 1 treats FPG/RPG > 18 as severe 'regardless of symptoms'. A notWhen that defers to a rule that cannot fire is a logic error; the missing box is treated as 'not unmet' with no gap. Rules 2 and 8.",
  "REFER-GLU-01: fire on glucose >= REF-DM-ACU-KETONE-TEST-GLU (or HI) after ketones are known, with glucose_goal_unmet_on_oral as a needsBeforeActing gap rather than a predicate, and run it for the newly found patient as well. CSO chooses between PEN ('refer all') and HEARTS-D section 4 ('no improvement after metformin and/or gliclazide'). RX-02/03/04's GLU18 notWhen must reference the same criterion.")
f("major", "40-stratify.json bp_systolic_who_hearts_d, bp_diastolic_who_hearts_d (H06: appliesTo not_pregnant); 50-act.json DM-ACT-REFER-BP-* (established_or_met)",
  "H06 removed the BP bands in pregnancy and nothing replaces them. Evaluator (own3 P19): 32-year-old, 30 weeks, fasting plasma 5.5 (WHO 2013 GDM met), BP 165/105 -> only DM-CON-PREG-01; no BP band, and the REFER-BP rules cannot run (not established, non-pregnant set not met). H06 test: pregnant type 1, BP 150/100 -> no BP signal.",
  "R3's H06 concerned glucose bands. A systolic of 160 or more in pregnancy is severe-range hypertension (pre-eclampsia risk, higher with diabetes); silencing the only BP display is a regression. Same-day antenatal referral (PREG-01, SCREEN-PREG-01) mitigates in part.",
  "Exempt the BP bands from H06, or add a pregnancy BP rule (diabetes in pregnancy with BP at or above the severe threshold -> same day/immediate) with thresholds from WHO's 2011 pre-eclampsia recommendations or UCG 2023 chapter 16 (CSO to supply).")
